      "definition": "used by a speaker or writer to refer to the person or people being spoken or written to",
      "explanation": "**You** has the same form for the subject and the object, and for one person or more than one; only the situation shows which is meant. The possessive determiner is **your**; the independent possessive is **yours**; the reflexive forms are **yourself**, for one person, and **yourselves**, for more than one.",
